# Releases no update may skip. A panel behind one installs it first, and the newest release on its
# next update, so each step runs the installer the step before it placed (install.sh
# _apply_update_stop; the Update card offers the same commit, system_ops._update_stop).
#
# Add a release here when the NEXT release depends on something it teaches the installed updater,
# the recovery command or the helper, which run from root-owned copies a release replaces only once
# it is installed. One line per release: its full commit id on main, then why. It must be a signed
# release (tools/sign-release.sh), or no panel will move to it. Read from the commit an update would
# install, so a stop added later counts for every panel whose installer reads this file.
#
# Only an updater that has this feature follows the list: a panel on an older release goes straight
# to the newest one, as before. A release added here does nothing for panels already past it.
